## GERMAISE'S BAKERY (`story.ni:4295-4383`) — the room; Germaise follows.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Bakery
  a room
  aka bakers shop, baker's shop, bakers, germaise's bakery, germaise's
  south to the Commerce Street, one-way

  The air is heavy with the warm and slightly damp smell of freshly baked
  bread, and the counters are piled high with golden loaves, baguettes, and
  rolls. You can leave the bakery to the south.

create the bread counter
  aka counter, counters, bakery counter
  scenery
  in the Bakery

  (TODO during play-testing — the counter has no description in the source;
  a line or none, David's call.)

create the bread
  aka baked goods, loaves, baguettes, rolls, loaf, baguette, roll, golden loaves
  scenery
  in the Bakery

  The bread looks and smells delicious, but right now you need answers more
  than you need a snack.

  on the player taking
    refuse bread-just-look
  end on

  on the player eating
    refuse bread-just-look
  end on

create the flour
  aka white powder, powder, powdery stuff, film of flour, thin film, dust, floury stuff
  scenery
  in the Bakery

  Germaise likes to throw around great handfuls of flour whenever he's making
  something, and he and everything else in the bakery is covered with the
  white, powdery stuff.

  on the player taking
    refuse flour-nothing-to-do
  end on

create the oven
  aka brick oven, huge oven, kiln, furnace, back wall, orange glow, glow
  scenery
  in the Bakery

  Most of the shop's back wall is actually the front of Germaise's huge brick
  oven. A warm, orange glow and the delicious smells of baking bread drift from
  its wide opening.

  on the player taking
    refuse oven-behind-counter
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse oven-behind-counter
  end on

  on the player opening
    refuse oven-behind-counter
  end on

## The source's "doing something other than examining" catch-alls, as the
## refusals a player is likely to reach for.

define phrase bread-just-look
  The bread looks and smells delicious, but right now you need answers more
  than you need a snack.
end phrase

define phrase flour-nothing-to-do
  It's just a thin film of flour — you can't really do anything with it.
end phrase

define phrase oven-behind-counter
  It's behind the counter, and Germaise wouldn't want you messing with it in
  any case.
end phrase

